# Session: 2026-06-17 (PM) — Anchor-mode doctrine: orbit ⇒ ref-only

**Topic:** Empirically proved (E10 A/B smoke) that on camera-orbit shots a pinned
`end_image` fights the orbit → ref-only is much better. Director verdict «с рефом
гораздо лучше». Redefined "Slice 3" = anchor-mode doctrine + regenerate-mode surfaces.
**A SHIPPED. B + C remain.**

---

## What We Are Building (the arc)

`episodes.metadata.generation_config` = FORMAT authority (Slice 1 video ✅, Slice 2 image ✅).
"Slice 3" was going to be per-shot FORMAT overrides — but exploration showed video plan-path
already honors per-shot via the Plan body, and image per-shot is YAGNI. Director pivoted to the
REAL axis: **per-shot anchor strategy** — two anchors (start+end_image, `seedance-with-end-image`)
vs ref-only (single anchor, `seedance-standard`, end_image=null).

**Empirical finding (THE anchor):** orbit + end_image = the camera hitches/morphs toward the
locked frame instead of arcing. ref-only renders much better. Since 80%+ shots orbit (TD-68),
**ref-only is the default; two anchors are the exception (STATIC non-orbit match-cut landing only).**
Memory written: `~/.claude/projects/C--SandyStudio/memory/anchor_mode_orbit_ref_only.md`.

---

